    "description": "Encapsulation is the practice of bundling data, in properties, and methods that operate on that data into a single unit, a class, while restricting direct access to some of the object's components. \n\nEncapsulation relies mostly on classes and visibility, to control access to data.\n\nThis is a fundamental principle of OOP, promoting security, modularity, and maintainability.",
